<title>USA: Hog disease cuts Taiwan corn import 500,000 T - USDA.</title>
<headline>Hog disease cuts Taiwan corn import 500,000 T - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan will import the smallest amount of corn in three years, 5.83 million tonnes, due to an outbreak of foot and mouth disease in its hog herds, U.S. Agriculture Department forecast Monday.</p>
<p>The import estimate was 500,000 tonnes lower than previously forecast for 1996/97.</p>
<p>&quot;The discovery of food and mouth disease on some Taiwanese hog farms has significantly impacted feed imports, specifically from the United States, as Taiwan is one of the top three markets for U.S. corn,&quot; USDA said in its monthly world grain report.</p>
</text>
